241 Cycles of the King of Kings handover had occurred. Each one went as smooth as was expected and no sign of trouble was showing. Yet when the <a href="naanuath-empire">Naanuath Emperor</a> was supposed to hand the title over to the Cuthage Emperor, he was nowhere to be found.

Over the preceding 200 cycles, the hand-off was held in Bannet's Antitower. At such an hand-off, every emperor had to be in attendance. Over time the meeting transformed from a meeting of friends to a high society ritual. 

Not in Bannet's Antitower, but in a palace far away, was the current Naanuath Emperor. Raganhar Gernot was convening with his closest allies and pondering the possible circumstances of the gambit they just played. When, at the time his reign ended and a hand-off was supposed to happen, the crown he still wore broke. The beautifully decorated crown, adorned with a jewel symbolizing each empire, shattered into ten pieces.

Inside Bannet's Antitower the Emperor had finally realized what just had occurred, when a shattered blackened crown appeared on the table. The crown was broken. The peace was broken.
